WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.464
Hi, I'm Daisy!

00:00:02.464 --> 00:00:05.204
MiMo-V2.6 Pro is a trillion-parameter open model.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:08.335
Here's how it's stored, trained and sped up.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:13.739
A trillion parameters in four bits, tuned by thirty RL steps, served

00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:16.687
with a drafter that fills eight slots at once.

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.342
Pro has seventy layers.

00:00:21.342 --> 00:00:25.495
Sixty see only a hundred and twenty-eight token window; ten are global,

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:26.880
buying back the reach.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.146
Each feed-forward holds three hundred and eighty-four experts, top eight, none shared.

00:00:32.146 --> 00:00:34.972
About forty-two billion parameters work per token.

00:00:35.392 --> 00:00:39.902
And the release is the four-bit checkpoint: five hundred and sixty-six gigabytes,

00:00:39.902 --> 00:00:41.405
not about two terabytes.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:47.448
The model card draws it: sliding-window blocks, then one global block, each

00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:49.502
with a sparse mixture of experts.

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:53.200
Image and audio encoders feed their tokens in, interleaved.

00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:59.177
The whole RL run is thirty optimizer steps, each on fifteen hundred

00:00:59.177 --> 00:01:01.504
and sixty-eight prompts, sixteen rollouts apiece.

00:01:01.924 --> 00:01:06.564
The router is frozen, so the experts re-tune inside the routing that pre-training learned.

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:10.722
Pass or fail can't rank two passing answers, so passing runs are

00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:13.214
ranked, and advantage shifts to the better ones.

00:01:14.675 --> 00:01:17.675
Fill the next eight positions with a mask token.

00:01:17.675 --> 00:01:22.007
A five-layer drafter reads them in one pass, guided by target hidden states.

00:01:22.427 --> 00:01:26.916
It drafts seven tokens, the target checks the block once, and keeps

00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:28.412
the longest matching prefix.

00:01:28.412 --> 00:01:29.908
Same quality, by construction.

00:01:30.328 --> 00:01:34.159
But a block is eight positions, so one target pass yields at

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:37.670
most eight tokens: eight times fewer passes, not the claimed twenty.

00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:43.388
What will last is the RL release: about seven thousand graded environments,

00:01:43.388 --> 00:01:44.803
each with its verifier.

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:52.083
To recap: four-bit weights, thirty RL steps, and a drafter capped at eight.

00:01:52.503 --> 00:01:54.620
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.225
I'm Daisy.

00:01:55.225 --> 00:01:55.527
Bye!
